  "prefLabel": "Alc 305.01 Examination Procedures",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Alc 305.01 Examination Procedures.\n\n(a) The examination required for initial certification as a CRSW shall be the IC&RC written “Peer Recovery” (PR) examination.\n\n(b) The examination required for initial licensure as a LADC shall be the IC&RC written alcohol and drug counselor (ADC) examination.\n\n(c) The examination required for initial licensure as a MLADC shall be the IC&RC written advanced alcohol and other drug counselor (AADC) examination.\n\n(d) The examination required for initial licensure as a licensed clinical supervisor shall be the IC&RC clinical supervisor (CS) written examination.\n\n(e) Candidates for examination shall register directly with the testing organization, including paying any fee(s) required by the testing organization, and request the testing organization to transmit the results directly to the licensing bureau as required by Plc 303.04.\n\nSource. #14584, eff 7-14-26, EXPIRES: 7-14-36",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/alc100-500.html"
